div.p:
To avoid the hiatus we could read (with Porson) τί μ᾽ οὖν;
                        but MSS. all give τί οὖν ; here, and Pers. 787, Theb. 704, 208: τί
                        εἶπας;
                        Trach. 1203, τι Ἅιδου Ag. 1115, τί ἔστι; Pers. 693: and the licence
                        with τί is quite intelligible.
